# Fugue Exposition for Solo Guitar (repertoire plan: st-fugue-exposition). An original fugue
# exposition in D minor for three voices on one guitar, in drop D tuning (string 6 down to D).
# Subject (bars 1-2, top voice alone): D D E F F G climbing in a dotted rhythm, then A Bb A G F E
# and the leading note C#. Answer at the fifth (bars 3-4, middle voice): the subject on A, in
# A minor (A A B C C D | E F E D C B G#), with the countersubject above it
# (C F E A | C A F D, all quarter notes: steady against the answer's dotted rhythm and its
# running eighths). Codetta (bars 5-6): the subject's rhythm turned downwards, back to D minor.
# Third entry (bars 7-8): the subject in the bass from the open low D, with the countersubject
# in the middle voice a fifth lower than before, and the top voice adding a few notes.
# The countersubject is written in invertible counterpoint: only thirds, sixths and octaves
# on the beats, so it works above the answer and below the subject alike.
# Then an episode built from the subject's head (bars 9-12), a dominant pedal on the open A
# (bars 13-16, the head climbing to G at fret 15), a fourth entry (bars 17-18: the subject in
# the middle voice over the open low D, the countersubject above it) and a close over the same
# pedal (bars 19-22), ending on D major. 22 bars in all.
# Held notes are ties (string:-): keep those fingers down while the other voices move.
# The chord symbols name the harmony the voices make; they are not strummed.
title: Fugue Exposition for Solo Guitar
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original fugue exposition for solo guitar
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 10
tags: fugue, counterpoint, three voices, drop d, d minor, baroque
tempo: 60
time: 4/4
key: Dm
tuning: drop-d

track: Your part
role: lead
